{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b971jyiok","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q1qyzxn7hANLJUUrM7i1P3","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/e8c1195f-6de5-4b1f-aa7e-fa673e50d32c/tasks/b971jyiok.output","summary":"Background command \"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; D=iter_0/candidate_0\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nPeople judge each sequence exactly as in the simplest current account (their own second-order model of a fair coin, with a person-specific believed switch rate, weighed against a switch-biased coin, a biased coin and a repeating short motif with slips, evidence per flip, person-specific sensitivity), but the decision rule has a person-specific lapse: on some share of trials, which differs from person to person, a participant does not judge at all and picks a side at random. This caps how often anyone agrees with the majority even on clear-cut pairs, so a subgroup of inattentive or near-random responders makes people's agreement with the majority vary more than graded sensitivity alone produces.\nEOF\necho person_lapse_second_order_chance > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc = open(\"models/second_order_chance_motif_suspicion.py\").read()\nhead, body = src.split('\"\"\"\\n\\nimport math', 1)\ndoc = '''\"\"\"Person-specific coin-flip lapse on the second-order chance-vs-motif judgment.\n\nHypothesis: people judge each sequence as in `second_order_chance_motif_suspicion`\n(their own second-order fair coin with a person-specific believed switch rate,\nagainst a switch-biased coin, a biased coin and a repeating motif with slips,\nevidence per flip, person-specific sensitivity), but on a person-specific share\nof trials lambda_i they do not judge and pick a side at random:\np_left = lambda_i / 2 + (1 - lambda_i) * sigmoid(eta). The lapse caps agreement\nwith the majority even on clear-cut pairs, so a subgroup of near-random\nresponders inflates the across-person variance of agreement.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math'''\nbody = body.replace('''    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta))''',\n'''    # Person-specific lapse rate (non-centred logit-normal population): on a\n    # share lambda_i of trials the person picks a side at random.\n    mu_lapse = pm.Normal(\"mu_lapse\", mu=-3.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_lapse = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_lapse\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_lapse = pm.Normal(\"z_lapse\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    lapse = pm.math.sigmoid(mu_lapse + sigma_lapse * z_lapse)[pid]\n\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\", 0.5 * lapse + (1.0 - lapse) * pm.math.sigmoid(eta)\n    )''')\nassert \"mu_lapse\" in body\nopen(\"iter_0/candidate_0/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(doc+body)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_0 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"fcc92760-cae7-4eb3-aa48-0149f28bc922","session_id":"e8c1195f-6de5-4b1f-aa7e-fa673e50d32c"}
